Hedging is an important financial concept that allows investors and traders to minimize various risk exposures. A hedge is effectively an offsetting or opposite position taken that will gain (or lose) in value as the primary position loses (or gains) value.

A hedge can be thought of as a type of insurance policy on an investment or a portfolio. These offsetting positions can be achieved using closely related assets or through diversification.

Among professional traders, the most common and effective hedge uses derivatives such as futures, forwards, or options contracts. is relevant
